<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4225" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλινδ-έω</span></b> , later <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλίνδω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, (pres. only in 
			Pass.
		): aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλῑσα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Nu.</u>
			32
		</span></i>, and pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤλῑκα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-</span>) ib.<i><span class="en">
			33
		</span></i> (the simple forms only in <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Suid.
		</span></i>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>make to roll.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, mostly in part., <i>rolling in the
			dust</i>, like a horse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλινδούμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.396e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλινδόμενοι ψαμάθοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					156
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλινδηθείς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				204
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλινδημένος</span>
			<i>rolled over, overturned</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; <i>to be twirled</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Iamb.</u>
				1.113
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>roam about</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλην ἐξ ἄλλης εἰς χθόν᾽
					ἀλινδόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.736
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλινδημένος ἐν αὐλαῖς
				σατραπικαῖς</span>
			<i>having grovelled</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Agis</u>
				3
			</span></i>; <i>frequent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τήν Ἀκαδημίαν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.14
				</span></i>
			; of money-lenders, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ περὶ τὰς
				ψήφους -ούμενοι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> sens. obsc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					5.30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
